{"id":"chatcmpl-fbe692a6-202f-42d9-b0eb-d86000582ffb","object":"chat.completion","created":1795245175,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task succeeds by delegating image interpretation to a domain-specific expert tool rather than reasoning directly from raw visual data. The key move is asking a targeted, anatomy-aware question that disambiguates between the two candidate findings (right vs. left hemidiaphragm elevation). The pattern generalizes to any binary visual-diagnosis task where a specialized tool can resolve ambiguity.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When a task requires interpreting specialized visual or domain data, route the question to a domain-specific expert tool instead of reasoning from raw inputs.\",\n    \"Frame the expert query to explicitly enumerate the candidate options and ask for the discriminating feature (e.g., which side, which structure), so the response maps cleanly to an answer choice.\",\n    \"Include anatomical/structural context cues in the query (view type, relevant landmarks, secondary signs) to improve expert reliability and reduce ambiguity.\",\n    \"After receiving expert output, map it directly to the option set and state the answer with the expert's reasoning as justification.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Visual diagnosis tasks\": \"Identify the discriminating feature between options, then ask a specialist tool a question that forces a choice on that feature.\",\n    \"Binary choice resolution\": \"Restate both options inside the expert query so the returned answer is directly mappable, avoiding post-hoc interpretation.\",\n    \"Tool-assisted reasoning\": \"Prefer one well-targeted expert call over multiple speculative calls; include view/context details that constrain the answer.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the expert query explicitly names the candidate options and the discriminating feature.\",\n    \"Verify the expert's returned finding maps unambiguously to exactly one answer option before finalizing.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":394,"total_tokens":753,"completion_tokens":359,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":394},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":359}}}